# Cursor Rules for audio-channel-queue-demo

## Project Overview
This is a demo frontend website for a TypeScript npm package for audio queue management with real-time progress tracking and event handling.

## Code Standards
- Use TypeScript with strict mode enabled
- All public functions must have comprehensive JSDoc documentation with examples
- All functions should show a return type
- All variable declarations (const and let) should show a return type (even basic ones like string or boolean)
- Object keys and imports should be alphabetically sorted
- Interfaces and types should be alphabetically sorted
- Interfaces that have the export prefix should be used in another file otherwise remove the export prefix if it's just used in it's own file
- Interfaces and types should be used at least one place in the repo and removed if they are not used
- CSS rules should be alphabetically sorted
- CSS classes should be alphabetically sorted
- CSS styling should be accomplished with as few rules as possible
- CSS classes that are not used should be removed unless they are color pallettes or part of a global ruleset
- Use modular architecture - keep concerns separated across files
- Return all time values in milliseconds for consistency
- Use consistent error handling with try/catch blocks
- Export interfaces and types from src/types.ts
- Remove all console.log() after you are done troubleshooting an issue

## Documentation
- Keep README.md examples current and functional

## Naming Conventions
- Use camelCase for functions and variables
- Use PascalCase for interfaces and types
- Use descriptive names that clearly indicate purpose
- Prefix callback types with the event name (e.g., ProgressCallback)

## Dependencies
- Minimize external dependencies
- Justify any new dependencies in commit messages
- Prefer native JavaScript/TypeScript solutions when possible
